# WHO THINKS WITH WHAT — the one place it is written. Every organ sources this.
#
# Owner ruling, 2026-11-11, verbatim: "we must resume these agents with managers
# being fable 5.2 and workers opus5.5 now that we have better models these can
# maybe do it as long as sone agents work on the system itself".
#
# Until that day it was the other way round, and by accident rather than design:
# the hourly builder ran on `fable` and the three desks on `opus`. Measured cost
# of that arrangement over 2026-09-06 .. 10-26 (usage_ledger.jsonl): the builder
# spent 253 weekly-meter points across 383 runs on the scarcest model, drove
# `week:Fable` to 100% while `week:all models` still had room, and lost 90 slots
# to model-specific limits. The organ that runs 24 times a day belongs on the
# model with the deepest pool; the organs that run once a day and decide what
# the other does belong on the best one.
#
# Aliases, not pinned ids, on purpose: `fable` resolved to claude-fable-5-2 and
# `opus` to claude-opus-5-5 when this was written (verified live, CLI 2.1.322),
# and the meter lookups in lib_usage.sh key on these names ("week:Fable"). When
# a better model ships the alias follows it and nothing here needs editing.
#
# A per-organ env override still wins (JACK_LOOP_MODEL, JACK_OVERSEER_MODEL,
# JACK_REVIEW_MODEL, JACK_FIELDWATCH_MODEL) — for one-off runs, not for policy.
MANAGER_MODEL=fable          # director (review.sh), overseer, field watch
MANAGER_FALLBACK=opus        # a manager that cannot get fable still sits, on opus
WORKER_MODEL=opus            # both worker lanes (ladder_loop.sh): jack and system
WORKER_FALLBACK="sonnet"     # NEVER fable: the worker must not drain the managers' pool

# WHICH CLAUDE PROGRAM RUNS — found by an independent audit the night of the
# reorganisation, and it would have quietly undone all of the above.
#
# Cron's PATH is /usr/bin:/bin. There `claude` is a root-owned npm install dated
# 2026-08-01 (CLI 2.1.220), whose aliases still mean the OLD models: `opus` ->
# claude-opus-5, `fable` -> claude-fable-5. The owner's shell finds
# ~/.local/bin/claude instead (the self-updating native build, 2.1.322 that
# night), where `opus` -> claude-opus-5-5 and `fable` -> claude-fable-5-2. So
# every hand test showed the new models, and the first cron-fired worker
# (21:07 UTC, 2026-11-11) ran on claude-opus-5 — measured from its transcript.
# The log said only "model opus". A control that reads a proxy for the thing it
# governs: the alias was checked, the program resolving it was not.
#
# So the program is chosen HERE, for every organ, and each start line prints the
# version it got. If the native build ever fails to start (a bad self-update
# while nobody is watching), the organ falls back to whatever `claude` the PATH
# already had rather than not running at all — older models beat a dark week.
JACK_CLAUDE_DIR=/home/opc/.local/bin
if "$JACK_CLAUDE_DIR/claude" --version >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  case ":$PATH:" in *":$JACK_CLAUDE_DIR:"*) ;; *) export PATH="$JACK_CLAUDE_DIR:$PATH";; esac
fi
CLAUDE_CLI="$(claude --version 2>/dev/null | head -1 | cut -d' ' -f1)"
CLAUDE_CLI="${CLAUDE_CLI:-unknown}"
